  <h2>Using the website information</h2>
  <p>
    The website explains DataDecision’s current methods and services. Public articles and templates
    provide general information. They are not legal or financial advice and do not guarantee a
    business outcome. A consultancy engagement begins under a separate written agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Service outcomes</h2>
  <p>
    AI-search visibility is sampled and changes with engines, prompts, sessions, locations and time.
    The service measures an agreed observation window; it cannot guarantee placement, citations,
    rankings, traffic, leads, pipeline or revenue.
  </p>

  <h2>Public methods and templates</h2>
  <p>
    You may use the public templates for internal evaluation. If you publish a measurement based on
    the method, include its date, sample, baseline, method version and relevant limitations.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and updates</h2>
  <p>
    Technical guidance is dated because provider policies and product behavior change. DataDecision
    corrects material errors when identified. Check the stated update date before relying on a
    technical note.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Do not misuse the site, interfere with its operation, submit unlawful material, impersonate
    another person or use the public contact path to send spam or malicious content.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    Articles link to provider documentation and other public sources. Those services control their
    own content, availability and terms. A link supplies evidence or context; it does not establish
    a partnership.
  </p>

  <h2>Commercial terms</h2>
  <p>
    Scope, fees, taxes, credit terms, confidentiality, intellectual property, payment timing,
    cancellation and liability are stated in the signed engagement agreement. That agreement governs
    the engagement.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:contact@datadecision.consulting">contact@datadecision.consulting</a> with questions
